      "evidence": "**Evidence:**\n- MEPS is expressly mandated: 42 U.S.C. \u00a7 299b-2 requires the AHRQ Director to \"conduct a survey to collect data on a nationally representative sample... on the cost, use and... quality of health care,\" with the content spelled out. The MEPS-IC ICR cites this statute as its authorizing law ([reginfo](https://www.reginfo.gov/public/do/PRAViewICR?ref_nbr=202506-0935-001)); the IC also operates under Title 13 via the Census Bureau.\n- Clear programmatic dependence: the IC supplies state and national employer-insurance spending estimates \"for the National Health Accounts and Gross Domestic Product\" ([90 FR 21308](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-05-19/html/2025-08862.htm)) \u2014 BEA/CMS depend on it.\n- No substitute exists: NHIS has no expenditure data; CPS/ACS lack cost and payment-source detail; claims data lack population denominators and the uninsured. Even the Trump administration's budgets and the FY27 request explicitly *protect* MEPS as core \"statistical work\" while cutting everything else around it ([FY26 budget, BUDGET-2026](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BUDGET-2026-BUD/pdf/BUDGET-2026-BUD.pdf); [AcademyHealth](https://ahsituationreport.substack.com/p/what-the-fy27-presidents-budget-request)).\n- Counterpoint (weak): a first-Trump-administration official suggested AHRQ's survey work \"could be done by others\" via contractors ([KFF Health News](https://kffhealthnews.org/health-industry/patient-safety-health-agency-dissolved-doge-federal-workforce-cuts-ahrq/)) \u2014 but that is about *who runs* the survey, not an alternative data collection.\n\n**Assessment: No Known Issue.** Explicit statutory mandate, prescriptive content requirements, irreplaceable function feeding federal economic statistics, and acknowledgment of MEPS's protected status even in hostile budget documents. (Note the statute obligates the *function*, which survives AHRQ's administrative dissolution \u2014 but the statute does not name a home division, which is why the Office of Strategy relocation is even possible.)\n\n---"
